  "description": "A-601 revises four doors' fire ratings. Tuesday's revisions of Door 106 and Door 107 from \"1.5 h\" to \"90 min\" are recorded as change stories, and Door 109's, also recorded, is approved on Tuesday evening. A Wednesday normalization of the project names the fixture fire-rating interpretation: chg-6 and chg-7 end on Wednesday by normalization, and chg-9, ended by its approval, is untouched. Door 108's Thursday revision, recorded after the normalization, has no period. On Thursday at noon Door 106 leaves the project, so its revision changes a property again: the disconnect act's write records the related change story chg-6+1, beginning then and citing the normalization in force until then. A Friday normalization of the project names literal comparison: its write records the related change stories chg-7+1 and chg-8+1, which begin on Friday citing the Friday normalization, list the revision's transitions, relate to the closed stories and await review. The closed stories stay ended, and chg-9, whose ending is a review, gets no related story. Pending review, open stories and what remains count each related change story.",
  "note": "7.3.8 *After it*: \"take the latest change story recorded for a revision (7.2.8), whose baseline ending is a normalization, as a period ending (7.2.7, 7.6.2) or as its no-period ending (7.6.12). When, at a later instant, the interpretation in force for its subject changes, through a later normalization, including one that returns to literal comparison, or through the subject joining or leaving a normalized scope, and the revision changes a property under the interpretation in force from then, maintenance records a related change story. Its detection carries `@relates_to` with an exact reference to the closed story's detection, and lists in `@transitions` the revision's transitions under the interpretation in force from that instant. Its period begins at that instant, it awaits review until an approval or a directive (7.2.7), and its beginning cites the normalization (7.6.4).\" 7.6.4: for `revision`, \"For a related change story of 7.3.8, the record is the normalization whose interpretation is in force from its beginning, or, where none is in force from then because the subject left the normalized scope, the normalization in force until then.\" README section 7 names the story `<prior story>+<n>` and dates its detection's context at the triggering record. chg-6+1 is outside the project from Thursday noon, so the project-scoped reads omit it.",
